From: Srinivas Kandagatla <srinivas.kandagatla@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:55:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/22] soundwire: stream: skip bps mismatch check for PDM
 streams

PDM data-port terminals carry a wire word length defined by the
stream payload, not by any host-side bps field; the bps declared by
slave and master need not agree.

Skip the sdw_config_stream() bps mismatch check for SDW_STREAM_PDM.
Behaviour for SDW_STREAM_PCM and SDW_STREAM_BPT is unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Srinivas Kandagatla <srinivas.kandagatla@oss.qualcomm.com>
(cherry picked from commit 63f2632d4d9f835a11841d0058655bfd18ae1578)
---
 drivers/soundwire/stream.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/stream.c b/drivers/soundwire/stream.c
index 9da62b5af228..456257058611 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/stream.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/stream.c
@@ -1400,7 +1400,9 @@ static int sdw_config_stream(struct device *dev,
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	if (stream->params.bps && stream_config->bps &&
+	/* PDM streams have no stream-wide bps; skip the match for them. */
+	if (stream_config->type != SDW_STREAM_PDM &&
+	    stream->params.bps && stream_config->bps &&
 	    stream->params.bps != stream_config->bps) {
 		dev_err(dev, "bps not matching, stream:%s %d vs %d\n",
 			stream->name, stream->params.bps, stream_config->bps);
